// What `cil:models` (xtask/src/cil/models.rs) accepts.
//
// - `unavailable`: classes the default models name that `model-run` cannot load, because they
//   are not part of .NET. Their generators are not checked.
// - `flows`: flows .NET shows that the models leave out on purpose, one entry per flow:
//   `fid` is a regex over the function id, `flow` is `src -> dst` in port spelling
//   (`Argument(0).\[] -> Return`), and `why` is required. An entry that matches nothing fails
//   the check (XPASS), so it goes when the model or the method changes.
{
  unavailable: [
    {
      cls: "[Newtonsoft.Json]Newtonsoft.Json.JsonConvert",
      why: "Newtonsoft.Json is a NuGet package, not part of the shared framework",
    },
  ],
  flows: [],
}
